; Inside an arithmetic expression, as outside one, a number's commas must
; group its integer part in threes after a leading group of one to three
; digits; otherwise the number is invalid and drops its transaction.
2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-01 open Assets:B

2020-01-02 *
  Assets:A  (1,2345) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-03 *
  Assets:A  (1,20 + 1) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-04 *
  Assets:A  (12,34,567) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-05 *
  Assets:A  1 + 1,20 USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-06 *
  Assets:A  2 * (3 + 1,23) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-07 *
  Assets:A  (1,234 + 1,000.50) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-08 balance Assets:A  2234.50 USD
